Pip Fizzlebang, a gnome warlock with goggles perpetually askew, trudged through the humid tangle of Stranglethorn Vale. Beside him floated Vex, his succubus, her emerald eyes scanning the jungle for humanoid targets. A troll patrol emerged from the brush. Pip grinned, whispering a command. Vex shimmered, vanishing into the foliage before reappearing behind the leader, her Lash of Pain crackling with shadow energy. The trolls fell quickly, but Pip’s mana was draining fast. He sighed, glancing at his empty health bar. "If only I had a Voidwalker to tank these hits," he muttered, wiping sweat from his brow. Vex sighed, her voice like velvet and smoke. "You chose style over survival, master." Pip shrugged, adjusting his goggles. "Style is survival in Stranglethorn."

The answer: Most warlocks use Voidwalkers because they provide essential tanking and threat generation, allowing the warlock to survive and manage aggro during questing and dungeon runs, whereas the Succubus is more specialized for crowd control and single-target damage. [end of text]


